## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

